  {
    "exam": "JEE Mains",
    "year": 2022,
    "session": "June",
    "subject": "Chemistry",
    "part": "1A",
    "topic": "Gaseous State",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "question": "Which amongst the given plots is the correct plot for pressure (p) vs density (d) for an ideal gas at different temperatures T1, T2, T3 (given T3 > T2 > T1)? (see diagram)",
    "questionImage": "gaseous easy/gs_easy_q2.png",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "(B)",
        "image": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "(A)",
        "image": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "(C)",
        "image": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "(D)",
        "image": ""
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "A",
    "explanation": "Explanation: Since pM = dRT => p = (RT/M) * d. Slope = RT/M. Since T3 > T2 > T1, the slope order is T3 > T2 > T1. Plot (B) shows T3 with highest slope, T2 intermediate, T1 lowest. Option A.",
    "explanationImage": "",
    "marks": 4,
    "negativeMarks": 1,
